WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:03.690
Lamp for reps. Part two: Engine leads.

2
00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:06.880
Where your calls come from, and how to work them.

3
00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:09.190
Click Engine leads.

4
00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:21.110
These are businesses our lead engine finds in public records, and scores. They're assigned to you. No other rep sees them.

5
00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:25.380
Every weekday morning, up to ten new ones arrive, and the bell tells you.

6
00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:30.970
Each row is one business. Let's go column by column.

7
00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:42.240
Tier is how strong the lead is. A means we found proof of both time in business and size. B means one of the two. Call A first.

8
00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:49.750
The number beside the tier is need, from one to three. Three means the strongest sign they need money now.

9
00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:56.130
Business is the company name, with its industry under it. Phone is the number to dial.

10
00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:58.730
Where is the city and state.

11
00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:05.030
Why is the most important column. It's the reason this business is on your list, and it's your opener.

12
00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:11.400
Prior MCA means a funder filed on them recently. They've taken an advance before, and may want another.

13
00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:18.510
NYC permits means they were just approved for big jobs. Materials and payroll go out before their client pays.

14
00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:24.590
An FMCSA fleet is an established trucking company, with ten to forty-nine trucks on the road.

15
00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:30.770
Signals lists the public records behind the lead, with dates. Found is the day the engine found it.

16
00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:35.810
Status is where you stand with the lead. Every lead starts at New.

17
00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:39.300
Called. No answer. Callback. Qualified.

18
00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:47.080
Called means you spoke to them. No answer, you didn't reach anyone. Callback, they asked you to call again.

19
00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:52.010
Qualified means they fit. A year or more in business, and real deposits.

20
00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:55.930
Submitted. Funded. Dead. Do not call.

21
00:01:56.320 --> 00:02:02.710
Submitted means their file went to funders. Funded means the money went out. Dead means not a fit.

22
00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:09.220
Do not call means they asked never to be called again. Respect it, every time.

23
00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:15.900
After every call, set the status. Lamp stamps the time, so the call counts in your numbers.

24
00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:23.260
Up top, filter by tier and status. Status starts on New, so leads you've worked drop off the list.

25
00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:29.120
Search finds any lead by name, phone, email, city or industry.

26
00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:33.480
Ready to apply? Tick the lead, and press Send application.

27
00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:45.390
Engine leads come from public records. They have a phone, but almost never an email. So ask for it on the call, and type it in.

28
00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:51.440
Then pick Email it. Lamp emails them their own link from the partners mailbox, and their replies come to you.

29
00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:57.480
When you send, Lamp saves the email on the lead, so it's there next time.

30
00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:04.210
No email yet? Pick Copy link, then Text it, to send the link from your own phone.

31
00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:06.470
Every good call ends with their email.

32
00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:13.940
Your target. 20 live conversations a day. Not dials. Conversations.

33
00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:18.170
Next: your files, stage by stage.
